-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Stored vote corrections — each cell named, each cell cited
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Generated by scripts/vr-gen-vote-corrections-migration.mjs from db/vr-vote-corrections-seed.json.
-- Do not hand-edit: regenerate, or roll forward with a new migration.
--
-- 18 stored member votes corrected across 8 roll calls · 15 members
-- house + senate · 0 votes created · 0 votes deleted · 0 roll calls, measures, mappings,
-- stated positions or profiles touched
--
-- WHERE THESE CAME FROM
-- The August 2026 attribution backfill re-read the official documents for every roll
-- call it filled, and re-checked the cells we ALREADY held against them as it went.
-- 7,931 stored cells agreed. These did not. The backfill was ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
-- throughout and deliberately refused to touch them, on the grounds that correcting a
-- stored vote is a deliberate act with its own citation. This is that act.
--
-- Most of them trace to attribution by inference in earlier seed waves — a member's
-- position filled in from a party's overall split rather than read off the roll — which
-- is exactly the failure mode that makes a not-voting member look like a voting one.
--
-- WHAT WAS VERIFIED BEFORE EACH LINE WAS WRITTEN
-- Every one of the 18 reported disagreements was re-checked from scratch by
-- scripts/vr-verify-vote-corrections.mjs: the roll call resolves to exactly one stored
-- row; the document identifies itself as that roll; the member is found in it by
-- published identifier (Bioguide via name-id for the House, LIS member id — confirmed
-- twice — for the Senate) and never by name; a fresh parse reproduces the official
-- position exactly; and the database still holds the value that was examined. A row
-- failing any of those is left alone and reported rather than corrected.
-- Verified: 18 · left uncorrected: 0
--
-- THE SHAPE OF THE CORRECTIONS
--    8 × stored yea → not_voting
--    5 × stored nay → not_voting
--    3 × stored yea → nay
--    2 × stored nay → yea
--   13 of the 18 move a member INTO present-or-not-voting, which is the direction
-- that matters most: a vote we recorded for someone who was not there is a sentence
-- about them that the record does not support.
--
-- is_party IS CORRECTED WITH THE POSITION
-- Where a member moves to not voting, is_party goes to NULL — no recorded vote, no side
-- to be with or against. Where the corrected position is a yea or a nay, is_party is
-- recomputed from that document's own party split, by the rule the backfill used.
--
-- IDEMPOTENT, AND FAIL-CLOSED
-- Each block reads the stored value first. It corrects only a cell still holding the
-- value the verification examined, treats a cell already holding the corrected value as
-- done, and RAISEs on a missing cell or on any third value — because at that point
-- something changed underneath this migration and it should stop, not overwrite.
--
-- Seed → member-map agreement: 18 cached politicianId(s) re-checked against
-- db/vr-member-map.json at generation time; 0 stale, 0 unresolvable.

DO $$
